# File: scripts/__tests__/test-layers-contract.test.mjs
# Generated from: specs/571-make-bdd-scenarios-the-single-acceptance-test-layer-with-a-kept-test-types-steering-setting/requirements.md
Feature: Make BDD scenarios the single acceptance test layer with a kept-test-types steering setting

  @SCN001
  Scenario: New specs task only scenarios and step definitions under the default
    Given a project with no steering/test-layers.json
    When /sdlc-write-spec generates tasks.md for an issue
    Then every AC-linked test task implements the feature.gherkin scenarios
    And no task asks for a separate test that restates an AC
    And variations of one AC are a Scenario Outline with Examples under that AC's @SCN tag

  @SCN002
  Scenario Outline: Kept-test-types setting is read and validated
    Given steering/test-layers.json is <state>
    When write-spec, the implement worker, or the verify worker renders its prompt
    Then <outcome>

    Examples:
      | state                                   | outcome                                                           |
      | missing                                 | the rendered rule names only bdd                                  |
      | {"version":1,"kept":["bdd","unit"]}     | the rendered rule names exactly bdd and unit                      |
      | {"version":2,"kept":["bdd"]}            | the render fails naming steering/test-layers.json and version     |
      | {"version":1,"kept":["bdd","e2e"]}      | the render fails naming steering/test-layers.json and kept[1]     |
      | {"version":1,"kept":["unit"]}           | the render fails naming steering/test-layers.json and kept        |

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Implement workers justify any non-scenario test
    Given an implement worker working an issue
    When it adds a test that is not a scenario's implementation
    Then the test is of a kept type and covers no scenario's behavior
    And the handoff lists it in justifiedTests with its type and justification

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Verify judges scenario coverage and flags duplicates
    Given an implementation under verify
    When the verify report is produced
    Then the Test Coverage section shows each AC's scenario and its implementation status
    And it flags branch tests that duplicate a scenario or have a non-kept type
    And it has no per-layer test count

  @SCN005
  Scenario: Testability checklist no longer rewards a second layer
    Given the verify testability checklist
    When an implementation is scored
    Then the injectable-clock and dependency-injection checks apply to step definitions and production seams
    And no score level rewards comprehensive unit tests or unit-test counts

  @SCN006
  Scenario: Setting is documented
    Given the README
    When a user reads the steering documentation
    Then it describes steering/test-layers.json, the type vocabulary, the BDD-only default, and how stages honor it
